---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const formalizeQuestionResult = await formalizeQuestion(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const inspectDataResult = await inspectData(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, formalizeQuestionResult.accepted);
const compileGraphResult = await compileGraph(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, inspectDataResult.accepted);
const executeAndAuditResult = await executeAndAudit(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, compileGraphResult.accepted);
const explainResultResult = await explainResult(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, executeAndAuditResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { formalizeQuestion: formalizeQuestionResult, inspectData: inspectDataResult, compileGraph: compileGraphResult, executeAndAudit: executeAndAuditResult, explainResult: explainResultResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...formalizeQuestionResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...inspectDataResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...compileGraphResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...executeAndAuditResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...explainResultResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...formalizeQuestionResult.checks, ...inspectDataResult.checks, ...compileGraphResult.checks, ...executeAndAuditResult.checks, ...explainResultResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A request says after without a time window: surface the consequential ambiguity rather than choosing one silently. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (surface the consequential ambiguity rather than choosing one silently.) through the existing stage result for AnalysisMeaning; preserve exact source/version and the prior AnalysisMeaning, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A one-to-many join inflates counts: enforce declared grain and cardinality checks. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (enforce declared grain and cardinality checks.) through the existing stage result for AnalysisMeaning; preserve exact source/version and the prior AnalysisMeaning, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A record is inaccessible to the requester: exclude it before model exposure and explain coverage without leaking it. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (exclude it before model exposure and explain coverage without leaking it.) through the existing stage result for AnalysisMeaning; preserve exact source/version and the prior AnalysisMeaning, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A rubric changes mid-run: pin the old run and create a targeted reclassification plan. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (pin the old run and create a targeted reclassification plan.) through the existing stage result for AnalysisMeaning; preserve exact source/version and the prior AnalysisMeaning, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A user changes only the grouping: reuse qualified row judgments and recompute exact aggregation. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (reuse qualified row judgments and recompute exact aggregation.) through the existing stage result for AnalysisMeaning; preserve exact source/version and the prior AnalysisMeaning, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, formalizeQuestion: formalizeQuestionResult, inspectData: inspectDataResult, compileGraph: compileGraphResult, executeAndAudit: executeAndAuditResult, explainResult: explainResultResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
